ness alright good now with  that out of the way let's move to  shocking fact number nine the author of  the hunt hunt manga yoshihiro tagashi  is married to naoko takeuchi the mangaka  of a little-known series you may have  heard of called sailor moon  so this is what we would call an  industry power couple and this is quite  relevant because after the conclusion of  sailor moon takeuchi became heavily  involved in hunt hunter which togashi  was just commencing and originally  takuchi played the role of togashi's  manager handling all sorts of office  administration before apparently being  fired from that position by her future  husband and at this point  she would put her artistic abilities to  use by colouring hunt hunter a task in  which takuchi was quite successful at  and was able to mimic togashi's art by  using the mantra of making her work as  ugly as possible  which worked very well actually her time  with the series didn't last past the  first volume though and the whole  tagashi takuchi relationship  is is quite a tumultuous affair with  takeuchi even calling their wedding off  on one occasion which has also led to a  fun internet joke about her wanting to  put their wedding on hiatus in the same  way that togashi would go on to  frequently put hunter hunter on hiatus  however things do seem to have worked  out in the end and the two are still  together to this very day after more  than two decades of marriage  so that's nice but let's refocus on  hunter hunter with shocking fact number  eight  tagashi may have already spoiled the end  of hunter hunter or at least the fates  of certain characters  quite specifically karapika and the  phantom troupe this is a now infamous  interview that occurred in volume 0  which is notable for being a prequel  focusing on krapika's life in the kurt  clan  prior to the phantom troop massacre in  any case amongst a slew of questions  contained as bonus material for the  volume tagashi was fairly blatantly  asked what will end up happening to  karapika  and the phantom troupe to which tagashi  quite plainly replied  they will all die and unfortunately  there was no follow-up question to that  so  this is what we have to work with and  this has led to a bit of division of  opinion in the hunt onto fanbase with  many believing that togashi's words were  intended as a joke  something that could very well be true  but is difficult to judge from printed  media whilst the other school of thought  is just to accept tagashi was telling  the truth and that the ultimate fates of  these tragic characters is to be erased  from this world it's an idea that  current manga events do support but only  time will tell  although even then let's be real maybe  time will decide to keep this one a  mystery however what is less of a  mystery is shocking fact number seven  the protagonists in hunter hunter all  have  mildly relevant birthdays or at least a  nice little feature where assumedly  coincidentally each protagonist of the  series is born on the same number  day that corresponds with that numbered  month of the year so for example  aorio was born on the third of march  thus making his birthday the third of  the third moving to krapika he has the  same thing going on being born on the  4th of april being the 4th of the 4th  and 1 month further we land on gon whose  birthday  is the 5th of may the 5th of the 5th  although this carries a bit of extra  relevance because the 5th of may is  actually a national japanese holiday  known as children's day and many child  protagonists of the manga realm have  that date assigned as their birthday but  skipping ahead to killwa he was born on  the 7th of july or the 7th of the 7th  however the most interesting part about  all of this  is that hisoka also fits quite nicely  into this trend having been born on the  6th of june or the 6th  of the 6th which is a key piece of  evidence used by fans when claiming that  hisoka is indeed  the fifth protagonist of hunter hunter  really intriguing stuff there but for  something just plain bizarre here is  shocking fact number six aunt hunter  spawned not just one but two  live-action musical extravaganzas now  that fact in itself isn't necessarily  strange in fact most mainstream anime  and manga tend to have a slew of  musicals dedicated to them in japan at  some stage or another but the hunt  hunter musicals well  they're particularly weird especially if  you've never seen hisoka's dance which  you should absolutely  look up on the youtube but the first  production is named musical hunter  hunter and it takes place theoretically  between the events of york new city and  greed island which basically sees the  core group on a mission to recover four  missing performers who each have  starring roles in an upcoming theater  festival meanwhile the second one would  be hunter hunter the nightmare of  zeoljec  because they spell zoldik the way the  data books do but this is uh  it's a sort of retelling of the zoltik  family arc although i think reimagining  might be a better word and it is  interesting because both illumi and  hisoka play major roles despite not  having been in the actual arc and what i  will say is someone who has worked in  musical theater for  most of their professional life is that  these shows are very paired back  productions minimal set basic lighting  and these shows are almost exclusively  carried by the performers which is very  much in line with traditional japanese  theater so look into them if you're keen  but speaking of keen we have shocking  fact number five  miss universe japan fantasies lyorio  alright a bit of background here we  are talking about yukimi matsuo who was  crowned as miss universe japan in 2013 a  year which now seems shockingly  shockingly far in the past but in  addition to being an actress a model and  competing in beauty pageants she is also  a passionate manga artist and all-around  lover of anime  manga and games in fact during the  japanese national contest she stated  that her ambition was to spread her love  for manga around the world  and she also went on to reveal that her  ideal man would be one  layorio from hunter hunter which i think  is a much needed win for laero in this  whole hunt under saga and it does make  some degree of sense given that he is  one of the few  characters in the series who you can  objectively consider something of a good  person given that his life is dedicated  to philanthropy and all i guess it's all  just a bit of a shame that he happens to  be you know  fictional though and as such he will  never get to know that he was  hand-picked by a miss universe  contestant no well no time for dwelling  on that now because we have shocking  fact number four the character of dwoon  is based on yoshihiro tagashi himself  and that's not  a flattering basis so if you're a more  casual fan just a quick recap dwin is  one of the game masters of greed island  and he is most notable for having his  name forcibly changed by jing in order  to fit the initial base naming scheme of  the title but when gone aces the trivia  section and officially beats the game he  is taken to dwin's room which is  portrayed as your typical hikokumori  existence  filled with but three things a man a  game  and an ass ton of garbage and this is  very much based in reality as togashi  has been known to adopt this lifestyle  from time to time and a very famous  picture exists of him playing dragon  quest in a room that can be best  described as a stye  and look full disclosure i'm not the  cleanest to people but this is too much  even for me and this photo is one of the  famed pieces of evidences for the lazy  tagashi argument portraying him as an  addicted gamer with no drive to actually  finish hunter hunter and while it's more  complicated than that there is no  denying that togashi does get wildly  absorbed into whatever singular focus he  has at any given time and the  culmination  of this personality in hunt hunter just  so happens to exist in dwin so that's  fun but moving on we now have shocking  fact  number three gone's arms are cursed not  literally of course which i do need to  point out because none curses are a  thing but in almost every arc gone ends  up suffering a grave injury to one of  his arms during the hunter exam his left  arm was quite brutally broken by hanzo  in the finals  in heaven's arena his right arm was  broken by guido's spinning tops then in  york new city the rider once again fell  victim to arm wrestling with nobunaga  but still that was probably quite  preferable to greed island where part of  his left arm was blown off entirely by  genthru's little flower although i will  remind you that this is a tactic that  gone had planned to occur because that's  what sane people do and then of course  in the chimera antarctic his right arm  was well and truly severed by  nephipito's post-mortem nen in fact the  only time gone's arms ever really get a  break in the series  pun intended is during the zoldic family  arc or i guess the election are but even  then his arm was shown as a withered  husk  it's just one of those motifs of hunter  hunter potentially designed to highlight  god's sheer recklessness  because these injuries never occur  accidentally they always happen because  gone is stubborn and rash in his  decision making but then again in the  complete opposite direction we move to  shocking fact number two the chimera  antarc  took seven and a half years to complete  and this does blow my mind somewhat but  the very first chapter of the chimera  antarctic entitled the queen  was released in june 2003 whilst the  last chapter titled  final will would not be released until  october 2011.  and that is quite the long slog i wasn't  reading at the time  nor had i watched the 1999 anime but i  can't help but feel for all of you  long-suffering hunter hunter fans during  this period it really does put  complaining about the pacing 